<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  CarPlay, as a voice-based conversational app (iOS 26.4+). Apple grants this by manual
  review, for this exact category, and an ungranted entitlement fails a build to SIGN rather
  than merely lacking CarPlay — so this file is wired into nothing: not CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS,
  not a build setting, and `ios/bin/testflight` refuses to sign it in. When the grant
  arrives: tick the CarPlay capability on the App ID, merge this key into the signed
  entitlements, admit it in the testflight guard, and check the first signed build with
  codesign (dump the entitlements of Zimmer.app) (a managed entitlement may need a manually made
  profile if cloud signing drops it). See ios/README.md, "CarPlay".
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.developer.carplay-voice-based-conversation</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
